# promise: #495
# A two-finger swipe over a Little Window's address bar goes where Back and Forward go, as over its
# page: on the first page, fingers to the right close the window (bensk on #495: "Could a swipe over
# the address bar work as well?"). The bar isn't the page, so Chromium's history swipe never sees it.
# cra://debug?littleBarSwipe= gives the bar's own scrollWheel the events a trackpad sends.
budget rss=700 stalls50=20
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)

cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?littleShown=open
expect-log little shown open: windows=1

# A short swipe, and one to the left (nothing ahead), leave the window open.
cra://debug?littleBarSwipe=short&fingers=right&points=30
expect-log little bar swipe short: none pages=1
cra://debug?littleBarSwipe=left&fingers=left
expect-log little bar swipe left: forward pages=1
wait 1
cra://debug?littleShown=kept
expect-log little shown kept: windows=1

# Fingers to the right on the first page close it.
cra://debug?littleBarSwipe=right&fingers=right
expect-log little bar swipe right: back pages=1
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleShown=swiped
expect-log little shown swiped: windows=0
